  "body": "1904 figures can hover above pavement where the rendered street masks out the raw terrain heightfield. This uses the existing walk, parkway, curb-top and alley triangles when both enabled terrain-cut materials prove that the raw field is hidden. Charles\u2019s measured ground height changes from 4.341757m to the drawn parkway at 4.311735m.\n\nOnly 1904 people use this support path. Water, decks, positive yard lifts and explicit stair/path heights retain their existing behavior. The horse roadway sampler and existing geometry remain unchanged. The lazy index adds 215,176 bytes and duplicates no XYZ data.\n\nValidation:\n\n- All 47 mask, material, Float32, deck/yard/water and fallback controls pass. An independent scan agrees with the actual district triangle index within 2.2e\u221213m; the original geometry and indices remain byte-exact.\n- Current-source canonical and focused controls passed in 16.68s under the original resource limits. All 976 foreign isolation rows and all 12 authored ungated reasons remain exact. One new gated tool updates the canonical counts.\n- The actual native-world observation at source `a1bc31a8` places Charles\u2019s root at the drawn parkway centre, 4.311735338m. All five runtime ground files are byte-exact in current source `facd6448`. Both compiled terrain-cut materials and all 1,466/1,476 foot-domain vertices were measured. Original horse assertions pass for that finite pose.\n- This corrects the ground height; full stance, gait and photographic acceptance stay open. Sole minima remain \u22122.315/\u22122.850mm on the slope. Conservative mask blend edges retain the raw field and may cause a height discontinuity.\n- The strict physical observer remains NONPASS because it recorded 30 native aborted requests. Actual page, HTTP, server and observer errors were zero. It closed in 376.18s under the original 600s cap with complete cleanup. The earlier attempt stopped at the original disk floor before measurement; that failure is preserved.\n\n[Earlier source, district and sparse-mask CPU evidence](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/tree/dae9ad71e2d7893696ff4dfcbb3fe96de231f1cc/evidence/transport/pedestrian-ground-2026-11-10/candidate-2c9) retains its exact source domain. The sparse six-pixel replay is not a reconstructed GPU mask. The measured world uses explicitly overlaid source, rather than a live current-head deployment. [Current-source controls and actual world measurements](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/tree/ec32be3e39d1ead21ff5144309d3ce5be9bb888c/evidence/transport/pedestrian-ground-2026-11-10/pr1921-facd6448) preserve the strict NONPASS and resource-floor recovery separately.\n\nThe owner authorized incremental PR-first checkpoints; complete local preflight remains UNRUN in this sparse asset checkout. Complete current-head hosted gates, moving frames and phone release remain required before DEV merge. T-2795 stays open for broader transport acceptance.\n",
